  "title": "Trump scales back U.S.-South Korea military drills amid North Korea's evolving strategy",
  "summary": "President Donald Trump orders the U.S. military to reduce joint exercises with South Korea, citing a'very good relationship' with North Korea, while North Korea's evolving battlefield tactics challenge the U.S. military's strategic position. This move, part of a series of annual exercises known as the Ulchi Freedom Shield, is seen as a counter to North Korea's evolving tactics.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "President Trump orders the U.S. military to scale back U.S.-South Korea military drills to address North Korea's evolving battlefield tactics.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "North Korea's North Korean official, Kim Yo-jong, criticized President Trump's claim that his brother Kim Jong-un responded to his outreach.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The drills, part of a series of annual exercises called the Ulchi Freedom Shield, are set to continue until August.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
